    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **53 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe membership level was computed inline in `OwnerMapper` and hard-capped at 3 (`Math.min(3, ...)`), so level 4 was unreachable.\n\n1. **New `MembershipLevels.of(owner)` helper** (`rest/function/common/MembershipLevels.java`) \u2014 keeps the existing pre-tenure factors (base 1, +1 for an email, +1 for `namesakeCount == 0`) capped at 3, then adds 1 for tenure. Tenure counts as qualifying only when `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(registrationDate, today) > 365`. So the max a new owner (zero tenure) can reach is 3, and level 4 is reserved strictly for owners registered more than 365 days ago.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 the `membershipLevel` mapping now delegates to `MembershipLevels.of(owner)`.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 raised the documented `maximum` from 3 to 4 and updated the description to spell out the tenure rule.\n\nThe `namesakeCount == 0` and email factors are the \"pre-tenure\" contributors that top out at 3; household size was never a formula factor (confirmed by Cp23, where a 3-member household member with no email stays at level 2), so the spec's \"3-member household\" phrasing is just illustrating a maxed-out new owner \u2014 still level 3, not 4. The new `Cp39Tests` (new owner capped at level 3) passes, and the existing level tests (Cp15, Cp23, Cp24) remain green.",
